{"status":"completed","summary":"Redis is persistently configured on node1 with an authenticated inventory identity. Its generated credential is stored at /etc/redis-inventory.env with root:root ownership and mode 0600. Redis and the stored test data recovered after a verified node reboot.","actions_performed":["Installed and enabled Redis 8.0.2.","Enabled AOF persistence with every-second fsync in /var/lib/redis.","Generated the inventory credential on node1; stored only its SHA-256 hash in the Redis ACL file.","Disabled unauthenticated access and verified the inventory identity can authenticate, read, and write.","Restarted node1 safely, confirmed its boot identity changed, and verified service and data recovery.","Generated missing SSH host keys after reboot and restored the enabled SSH service, returning system state to running."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Redis persistent storage","command_ids":["cmd-79e1660d00ee4550","cmd-b3fd47d7a6db4b18","cmd-e1c3a849c57d4862"],"summary":"Configuration shows AOF enabled with every-second fsync; runtime reports healthy AOF files and the durable value survived the node reboot."},{"requirement":"Dedicated inventory application identity","command_ids":["cmd-d998ee78c63d46d8","cmd-b3fd47d7a6db4b18","cmd-e1c3a849c57d4862"],"summary":"Shows the inventory ACL, denied anonymous access, authenticated PONG, ACL WHOAMI=inventory, and successful data access before and after reboot."},{"requirement":"Generated credential stored root-only in /etc/redis-inventory.env","command_ids":["cmd-d998ee78c63d46d8","cmd-b8f38445c89e4359","cmd-e1c3a849c57d4862"],"summary":"Shows the expected environment fields and confirms mode 0600 with root:root ownership before and after reboot without exposing the credential."},{"requirement":"Redis service availability and automatic startup","command_ids":["cmd-0926e3916aa54087","cmd-e1c3a849c57d4862"],"summary":"Redis is active, enabled, ready, and listening on node1's managed IP before and after reboot."},{"requirement":"Mandatory node1 restart and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-b8f38445c89e4359","cmd-83872371b73d4d0b","cmd-fc63da3f09d24869","cmd-e1c3a849c57d4862"],"summary":"Captures the healthy baseline and original boot ID, acknowledged native reboot, changed boot ID, running system state, recovered Redis identity, persistence status, and durable data."},{"requirement":"Post-restart platform service recovery","command_ids":["cmd-2bb42e4fbac742ce","cmd-0e254cdae288404d","cmd-e1c3a849c57d4862"],"summary":"Diagnosed missing SSH host keys, generated them natively, restored SSH, and confirmed the overall system state is running."}]}
